From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] contacts: buttons to call a contact and to edit it
Description:
 Each entry of the contacts page gets a button that calls the contact
 right away and a button that opens the contacts application (Plasma
 Phonebook, started through KIO) to edit it; a tap on the entry still puts
 the number into the dial pad. For a contact with several numbers the
 number is asked for first. Plasma Phonebook has no way to be asked for a
 given contact, so the edit button starts it on its list of contacts; the
 button is disabled when it is not installed.
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (LGPL-2.0-or-later, LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL); new files contactsapp.* LGPL-2.0-or-later
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
---
--- a/plasma-dialer/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/plasma-dialer/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL
 
 set(dialer_SRCS
+    contactsapp.cpp
     lockscreenutils.cpp
     ringtoneutils.cpp
 )
@@ -43,7 +44,7 @@ qt_target_qml_sources(plasma-dialer QML_FILES
 
 
 find_package(Qt6 ${QT_MIN_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED Core Quick Qml QuickControls2 Multimedia)
-find_package(KF6 ${KF_MIN_VERSION} REQUIRED COMPONENTS Config Crash CoreAddons I18n DBusAddons)
+find_package(KF6 ${KF_MIN_VERSION} REQUIRED COMPONENTS Config Crash CoreAddons I18n DBusAddons KIO Service)
 find_package(KF6KirigamiAddons 1.3 REQUIRED)
 
 if (DIALER_BUILD_SHELL_OVERLAY)
@@ -83,6 +84,8 @@ target_link_libraries(plasma-dialer PRIVATE
     KF6::I18n
     KF6::I18nQml
     KF6::DBusAddons
+    KF6::KIOGui
+    KF6::Service
 )
 if (DIALER_BUILD_SHELL_OVERLAY)
     target_link_libraries(plasma-dialer PRIVATE
--- /dev/null
+++ b/plasma-dialer/src/contactsapp.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.0-or-later
+
+#include "contactsapp.h"
+
+#include <KIO/ApplicationLauncherJob>
+#include <KService>
+
+#include <QDebug>
+
+static const QString contactsAppName = QStringLiteral("org.kde.phonebook");
+
+ContactsApp::ContactsApp(QObject *parent)
+    : QObject(parent)
+{
+}
+
+bool ContactsApp::available() const
+{
+    return KService::serviceByDesktopName(contactsAppName) != nullptr;
+}
+
+void ContactsApp::open()
+{
+    const KService::Ptr service = KService::serviceByDesktopName(contactsAppName);
+    if (!service) {
+        qWarning() << "Could not find the contacts application" << contactsAppName;
+        return;
+    }
+    auto job = new KIO::ApplicationLauncherJob(service);
+    job->start();
+}
